Subject: [candidate] preserve owned primary-token references in the Wine kernel-object model

Experimental, isolated guest-compatibility implementation. Resolve only a retained
process object already mapped by a manager owned by this address space. The
operation holds the actual server token object; it creates no token handle,
accepts no PID or access mask, grants no user query/adjust rights and leaves
ordinary access checks unchanged. No host-token substitution, anti-cheat change
or game-gate change. Not selected by recipes; native conformance is pending.
Applies after 0018 and requires matching regenerated protocol/ntdll/server.

